Virtualmin Core Patches for Remote Mail Plugin Integration
==========================================================

These patches modify Virtualmin's virtual-server module to support plugin-
provided users in the main users listing.

Upstream PR: https://github.com/virtualmin/virtualmin-gpl/pull/1183

Once merged, these patches will no longer need to be applied manually after
Virtualmin updates.

All patches gracefully degrade — if no plugins define the hooks, the code
is a no-op and behavior is identical to stock Virtualmin.


Files
-----

virtual-server/list_users.cgi
    Full patched file. Replaces the hardcoded "Add Remote Mail User" link
    with a generic plugin hook (users_create_links). Any feature plugin
    can now add user creation links to the users page.

virtual-server/virtual-server-lib-funcs.pl.patch
    Unified diff for the two changes to virtual-server-lib-funcs.pl
    (file is ~22000 lines, too large to store in full):

    1. list_domain_users() — Adds a list_plugin_users hook after the
       existing virtualmin-htpasswd web users block. Feature plugins
       can return extra user hashes to be merged into the users table.

    2. users_table() — Adds edit_url support. If a user hash contains
       an 'edit_url' key, that URL is used for the user's name link
       instead of the default edit_user.cgi link. This lets plugin
       users link to their own edit pages, and works in both GPL and
       Pro editions.


Plugin-Side Hooks (in virtual_feature.pl)
-----------------------------------------

list_plugin_users(&domain)
    Returns a list of user hashes for remote mail users. Each hash has:
    - user, email: user@domain.tld
    - real: "Remote mail" type label
    - extra: 1 (marks as non-Unix user)
    - type: module name
    - edit_url: link to plugin's edit_domain.cgi
    - noquota, noprimary, noextra, noalias, nocreatehome, nomailfile: 1

users_create_links(&domain)
    Returns an array of link arrays for the "Add" buttons:
    [ "/virtualmin-remote-mail/edit_user.cgi?dom=...", "Add Remote Mail User" ]


Applying Patches
----------------

On the Virtualmin server:

    # list_users.cgi — copy the full file
    cp patches/virtual-server/list_users.cgi \
       /usr/share/webmin/virtual-server/list_users.cgi

    # virtual-server-lib-funcs.pl — apply manually using the .patch
    # file as a guide (line numbers may shift with Virtualmin updates)

After a Virtualmin update, check if the patches are still present:

    grep -n 'list_plugin_users' \
        /usr/share/webmin/virtual-server/virtual-server-lib-funcs.pl
    grep -n 'users_create_links' \
        /usr/share/webmin/virtual-server/list_users.cgi
    grep -n 'edit_url' \
        /usr/share/webmin/virtual-server/virtual-server-lib-funcs.pl

If any are missing, re-apply. The patches/ directory preserves the exact
code needed.
